# JARDIM alone, a win: the three labyrinths and the final enemy, touched at 79870
# (lives 3, health 115, 2100 points). The route is the probe-driven planner's (docs/jardim/DESIGN.md "Tests"): presses only
# (`hold KEY 1`, 30 ms apart: a 16-unit step or a 48-unit turn each, no tick while a key
# is down), two presses a cell along the axes; it shoots every Bussuf (crossbow) and
# Alemao in its line ahead, walks around Seios, Siri, Bicho and Chato, opens the doors on
# its way (SPACE) and takes the exit doors.
# The same game in both versions (J2-J6 never act on it; J4 changes the pictures); the
# result differs by BUGS.md J1: the Original's "bonus" divides 10^9 by the low tick word
# less the start tick (0 alone: +4228, won 6328), the Corrigida's by the milliseconds
# played (+12520, won 14620).
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame jardim --headless --ms 82000 --input tools/play/jardim-alone-win.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame jardim --headless --ms 82000 --fix all --input tools/play/jardim-alone-win.input
